# nanopb sizing for the cluster-sync messages (docs/CLUSTER-SYNC-M4.md §3).
#
# payload: ONE FRAGMENT of an encoded meshtastic.Config section, NOT the whole
# entry payload -- those are two different caps now (agents-ooma.36). What a
# document entry may hold is MESHTASTIC_CLUSTER_PAYLOAD_MAX, a RAM/NVS choice;
# what fits one frame is this, a wire fact. Before fragmentation they had to be
# the same number and the BUILD_ASSERT in meshtastic_cluster.c tied them.
#
# 88 is the largest value that leaves a signed last fragment inside the frame
# budget. The arithmetic, since it is not obvious and is easy to erode:
#
#   budget        ClusterMessage_size + 16 <= 233   =>  ClusterEntry <= 214
#   fixed cost    key 16 + stamp 25 + tombstone 2                     43
#   fragmentation payload_total 6 + frag_offset 6                     12
#   signature     author_sig, on the last fragment only               66
#   fragment      this cap + tag + len                            88 + 2
#                                                              --------
#                                                                    211
#
# The key and stamp are in every fragment on purpose (see cluster.proto), which
# is what makes the 43 a per-FRAGMENT cost rather than a per-entry one. Raising
# this cap costs frame budget one-for-one; the BUILD_ASSERT is what notices.
*ClusterEntry.payload    max_size:88

# The author signature over a reassembled entry. Ed25519, so this is not a
# tunable -- 64 is the signature size.
*ClusterEntry.author_sig max_size:64

# 4 rows x 43 B (generated KeyStamp_size 41 + repeated overhead) keeps a full
# ClusterVector inside one frame's Data budget; larger documents resume via
# offset/total. The BUILD_ASSERT on ClusterMessage_size in meshtastic_cluster.c
# is what keeps these counts honest against the generated sizes.
*ClusterVector.entries   max_count:4
*ClusterEntryReq.keys    max_count:6

# Firmware intent: 4 classes covers this fleet twice; a row is ~18 B, so a full
# FleetIntent is ~72 B -- inside MESHTASTIC_CLUSTER_PAYLOAD_MAX (128) as an
# entry, and inside the 88-byte fragment cap above, so the fleet's own intent
# still travels in a single frame.
*ClassIntent.hash_prefix max_size:4
*FleetIntent.rows        max_count:4
